{"judgments": [
  {"clause_id": "c001",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"Common texts or twin texts\" is used as the limit on the form's use but is nowhere defined in the instrument, and the sentence's broken syntax leaves the restriction's reach unclear. A user could not tell from these words which submissions the form may or may not cover.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.27},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.11}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c002",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"Implied license grant\" is a term of art capable of more than one reading: it may deny only that a license passes automatically by implication, or may deny that any licensing obligation arises at all. The disclaimer's scope is exactly what a licensee and patent holder would read differently.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.42},
     {"issue": "This disclaimer sits against the Option 2 commitment (c003) that \"The Patent Holder will grant a license to an unrestricted number of applicants\"; one text denies any grant while the other promises one. A court must reconcile a binding promise to license with a statement that the declaration grants nothing.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.55}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c003",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"Reasonable terms and conditions\" and \"non-discriminatory basis\" set no benchmark, rate, or method of determination, so the content of the promised licence is indeterminate. Two parties can and do read the same RAND words to require very different royalties.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.78},
     {"issue": "The unqualified promise that the holder \"will grant a license\" cannot be squared with the accompanying statements that \"This declaration does not represent an implied license grant\" (c002) and that \"Negotiations of licenses are left to the parties concerned\" (c004). Whether this is a binding obligation to license or only an undertaking to negotiate turns on harmonising those texts.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.60}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c004",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"Left to the parties concerned\" does not say whether negotiation is merely relocated outside the standards bodies or is a precondition to any licensing duty. The phrase is the hinge of the \"obligation to grant versus obligation to negotiate\" argument.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.44},
     {"issue": "It is in tension with the Option 2 undertaking (c003) that the holder \"will grant a license ... on reasonable terms and conditions\": if terms are wholly for negotiation, the RAND promise has no independent content. A court would have to decide which text controls.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.55}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c005",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"Willing to license their patents or patent claims under options 1 or 2\" leaves open how willingness is demonstrated and whether the counterparty's patents must be essential to the same standard. The condition's trigger is therefore not self-applying.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.33},
     {"issue": "The reciprocity condition qualifies the Option 2 promise (c003) to license \"an unrestricted number of applicants,\" and the two are hard to read together without deciding which applicants may be refused. That interaction is a genuine construction point.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.31}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c006",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"Does not represent an actual grant of a license\" may mean only that no licence passes on the form, or may mean that no enforceable licensing obligation is created. The scope of the disclaimer is the whole dispute.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.44},
     {"issue": "It stands against the checked Option 2 statement (c007) that the holder \"is prepared to grant a license ... on reasonable terms and conditions,\" the very obligation this sentence appears to disclaim. Harmonising the two requires construing the instrument as a whole.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.55}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c007",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"Reasonable terms and conditions\" on a \"non-discriminatory basis\" fixes no royalty, no ceiling and no mechanism, so the licence's content is left indeterminate on the face of the text. That indefiniteness is precisely what opposing parties construe differently.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.80},
     {"issue": "\"Is prepared to grant\" is ambiguous between a binding promise to grant and a mere statement of present willingness to negotiate. The choice between those readings decides whether the declaration is enforceable at all.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.66},
     {"issue": "The commitment cannot be squared as written with the form's own heading that \"This declaration does not represent an actual grant of a license\" (c006) and the negotiations sentence (c008). A court must decide whether those texts qualify or defeat the Option 2 promise.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.57}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c008",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"Negotiations are left to the parties concerned\" does not state whether it merely allocates the forum for negotiation or makes negotiation the entire extent of the holder's duty. The phrase supports two competing readings on its face.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.44},
     {"issue": "It pulls against the Option 2 commitment (c007) to grant licences on reasonable and non-discriminatory terms, since unconstrained negotiation would drain the RAND undertaking of content. Reconciling the two is a whole-instrument question.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.54}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c009",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The clause imports \"reciprocity\" as a condition on willingness to license without stating who must reciprocate or when, relying entirely on the separate definition. Whether the condition is a precondition to any offer or only a permitted licence term is not resolved here.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.31},
     {"issue": "The condition qualifies the Option 2 promise (c007) to license \"an unrestricted number of applicants,\" and the two provisions must be read together to know which applicants may be refused. That is a live reconciliation problem within the same form.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.33}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c010",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"Other reasonable terms and conditions such as those relating to governing law, field of use, reciprocity, warranties, etc.\" places an open-ended \"etc.\" after a short enumerated list, leaving the catch-all's reach uncertain. How far beyond the named categories a patent holder may impose terms is exactly the ejusdem generis question.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.38},
     {"issue": "The free-of-charge definition explains a term used only in Option 1, which is unchecked in this declaration where Option 2 (c007) is selected, so its operative effect on this declaration is unclear. A party could argue it colours the meaning of \"reasonable terms and conditions\" in the checked option.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.22}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c011",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The definition conditions the duty on the licensee committing to license \"free of charge or under reasonable terms and conditions\" without saying how or when that commitment must be made. The threshold for satisfying reciprocity is therefore not self-applying.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.34},
     {"issue": "Read with the reciprocity checkbox (c009) and the Option 2 promise to license \"an unrestricted number of applicants\" (c007), it is unclear whether a non-reciprocating implementer is outside the commitment entirely. That interaction requires construction of the form as a whole.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.30}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c012",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"Does not represent an actual grant of a license\" may deny only the automatic passing of a licence or may deny any enforceable licensing duty. The breadth of that disclaimer is genuinely contestable.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.43},
     {"issue": "It conflicts in appearance with the checked Option 2 undertaking in the same form (c013) that the holder \"is prepared to grant a license ... on reasonable terms and conditions.\" A court would have to decide whether the disclaimer defeats or merely qualifies that undertaking.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.54}
   ]}
]}

